  - CHANGELOG.md
learnings:
  - The moat feature's data was already fully present — the calibrate writer persists LearnedBand{min,max,n} with MIN_SAMPLES=8 as the graduation bar, and the learned table only ever contains graduated cells. resolveAgentEstimate just discarded n+source. The 'big data-wiring' the design feared was a 4-line widening, not a writer change. Verify the actual data shape before scoping a dependency as expensive.
  - This project has never run `paradigm calibrate`, so every estimate is source:prior (cold-start). The UI MUST render the all-prior state honestly (dimmed ~prior~) — that IS the correct first-run experience, and it's what proves the LEARNED path will light up as actuals accumulate. Tested both states in unit tests since live data can't show the learned path here.
  - estimateForTask takes the PRE-LOADED learned table (not a rootDir) so a route attaching estimates to N tasks reads token-estimates.json once, not N times.
